<h1>Gemma 4 31B-IT Deployment Analysis via AEX Model Service</h1>

<table class="info-table">
<tr><td>User Story</td><td>2748133 - Explore deployment of Gemma model</td></tr>
<tr><td>Model</td><td>google/gemma-4-31b-it</td></tr>
<tr><td>Sprint</td><td>Cat Digital 2026 | Sprint 12 (Jun 10 - Jun 23)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Owner</td><td>Sowndarya Kurapati</td></tr>
<tr><td>Date</td><td>June 18, 2026</td></tr>
<tr><td>AWS Region</td><td>us-east-2 (Ohio)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Pricing Type</td><td>On-Demand</td></tr>
</table>


<h2>1. Model Specifications</h2>
<table>
<tr><th style="width:35%;">Specification</th><th style="width:65%;">Value</th></tr>
<tr><td>Model Name</td><td>google/gemma-4-31b-it</td></tr>
<tr><td>Parameters</td><td>31 Billion (Dense)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Model Size on Disk (BF16)</td><td>~65 GB</td></tr>
<tr><td>VRAM Required (FP16/BF16)</td><td>~71 GB</td></tr>
<tr><td>VRAM Required (NVFP4 Quantized)</td><td>~45 GB</td></tr>
<tr><td>Minimum GPU</td><td>1x NVIDIA A100 80GB or 2x A100 40GB (tensor parallel)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Recommended Serving Engine</td><td>vLLM v0.8.0+</td></tr>
<tr><td>Context Length</td><td>Up to 256K tokens</td></tr>
<tr><td>Source</td><td>JFrog Artifactory (artifacts.cat.com) - Approved</td></tr>
<tr><td>Artifactory Path</td><td>cat-huggingface-repo/models/google/gemma-4-31B-it/</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>2. AWS Deployment Options via AEX Model Service</h2>
<p>The CMAAI-Model-Service GitHub Actions workflow supports the following AWS deployment paths for Gemma 4 31B:</p>
<table>
<tr><th style="width:5%;">#</th><th style="width:25%;">AWS Service</th><th style="width:15%;">AEX model-type</th><th style="width:15%;">Can Deploy?</th><th style="width:40%;">Primary Blocker</th></tr>
<tr><td>1</td><td>Amazon SageMaker</td><td>sagemaker</td><td class="warn">MAYBE</td><td>65 GB tar.gz packaging; no GPU instance selection</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td>Amazon ECS on EC2 (GPU)</td><td>huggingface</td><td class="fail">NO</td><td>Storage 20 GiB &lt; 65 GB; ECR 52 GB limit; No GPU on Fargate</td></tr>
<tr><td>3</td><td>Amazon Bedrock</td><td>N/A</td><td class="fail">NO</td><td>Gemma 4 not available on Bedrock (only Gemma v3)</td></tr>
<tr><td>4</td><td>LLM Object</td><td>llmobject</td><td class="warn">UNKNOWN</td><td>Undocumented - needs investigation</td></tr>
</table>


<h2>3. OPTION 1: Amazon SageMaker (model-type = "sagemaker")</h2>
<p><b>How It Works:</b> Model is packaged as model.tar.gz, uploaded to Amazon S3, and deployed to a SageMaker real-time inference endpoint.</p>

<h3>Feasibility Assessment</h3>
<table>
<tr><th style="width:25%;">Requirement</th><th style="width:30%;">AWS Capability</th><th style="width:25%;">Gemma 4 31B Needs</th><th style="width:20%;">Status</th></tr>
<tr><td>Model packaging</td><td>S3 multipart upload, no size limit</td><td>65 GB tar.gz</td><td class="warn">POSSIBLE but slow</td></tr>
<tr><td>Endpoint storage</td><td>Configurable EBS volume</td><td>65+ GB</td><td class="pass">PASS</td></tr>
<tr><td>GPU availability</td><td>ml.g5, ml.p4d, ml.p5 families</td><td>A100 80GB min for FP16</td><td class="pass">PASS</td></tr>
<tr><td>Cold start</td><td>Instance launch + model load</td><td>5-15 minutes</td><td class="warn">SLOW</td></tr>
<tr><td>Inference timeout</td><td>60 seconds max (real-time)</td><td>Depends on output</td><td class="warn">RISK</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Problems Blocking This Path</h3>
<table>
<tr><th style="width:5%;">#</th><th style="width:25%;">Problem</th><th style="width:50%;">Detail</th><th style="width:20%;">Severity</th></tr>
<tr><td>1</td><td>No staging infrastructure</td><td>Need a server to download 65 GB from JFrog, compress to tar.gz, and upload to S3. No such server exists today.</td><td class="critical">CRITICAL</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td>65 GB tar.gz impractical</td><td>Safetensors files do not compress well. Creating tar.gz takes hours and output is nearly same size.</td><td class="high">HIGH</td></tr>
<tr><td>3</td><td>No GPU instance selection</td><td>Workflow only has deploy-on-gpu=true/false. Cannot specify ml.p4d.24xlarge or ml.g5.12xlarge.</td><td class="high">HIGH</td></tr>
<tr><td>4</td><td>No JFrog-to-S3 transfer</td><td>No automated pipeline to move 65 GB from Artifactory to S3. Lambda limited to 10 GB.</td><td class="high">HIGH</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Amazon SageMaker Instance Pricing - us-east-2 (Ohio) On-Demand</h3>
<div class="disclaimer"><b>IMPORTANT:</b> SageMaker pricing below is derived from cloudprice.net monthly rates (divided by 730 hours). Verify exact pricing at aws.amazon.com/sagemaker/pricing - select "US East (Ohio)" region.</div>
<table>
<tr><th style="width:16%;">Instance</th><th style="width:5%;">GPUs</th><th style="width:12%;">GPU Type</th><th style="width:10%;">Total VRAM</th><th style="width:12%;">Can Run?</th><th style="width:5%;">TP</th><th style="width:12%;">$/Hour*</th><th style="width:14%;">$/Week (168h)</th><th style="width:14%;">$/Month (730h)</th></tr>
<tr><td>ml.g5.12xlarge</td><td>4</td><td>NVIDIA A10G</td><td>96 GB</td><td class="warn">Quantized only</td><td>TP=4</td><td><b>$7.09*</b></td><td>$1,191.12</td><td>$5,175.70</td></tr>
<tr><td>ml.g5.48xlarge</td><td>8</td><td>NVIDIA A10G</td><td>192 GB</td><td class="pass">Yes</td><td>TP=4</td><td><b>$20.36*</b></td><td>$3,420.48</td><td>$14,862.80</td></tr>
<tr><td>ml.p4d.24xlarge</td><td>8</td><td>NVIDIA A100 40GB</td><td>320 GB</td><td class="pass">Yes</td><td>TP=2</td><td><b>$25.25*</b></td><td>$4,242.00</td><td>$18,433.44</td></tr>
<tr><td>ml.p4de.24xlarge</td><td>8</td><td>NVIDIA A100 80GB</td><td>640 GB</td><td class="pass">Yes (1 GPU)</td><td>TP=1</td><td><b>$31.56*</b></td><td>$5,302.08</td><td>$23,041.80</td></tr>
<tr><td>ml.p5.48xlarge</td><td>8</td><td>NVIDIA H100 80GB</td><td>640 GB</td><td class="pass">Yes (fastest)</td><td>TP=1</td><td><b>$63.29*</b></td><td>$10,632.72</td><td>$46,206.08</td></tr>
</table>
<p><i>* Hourly rate derived from cloudprice.net monthly pricing. Verify at AWS SageMaker pricing page.</i></p>
<p><b>Verdict: MOST VIABLE AEX PATH</b> - Requires solving file transfer and tar.gz packaging challenges first.</p>


<h2>4. OPTION 2: Amazon ECS on EC2 with GPU (model-type = "huggingface")</h2>
<p><b>How It Works:</b> Model artifacts in Amazon S3 are pulled to an ECS worker node and loaded into GPU memory for inference.</p>

<h3>Problems Blocking This Path</h3>
<table>
<tr><th style="width:5%;">#</th><th style="width:25%;">Problem</th><th style="width:50%;">Detail</th><th style="width:20%;">Severity</th></tr>
<tr><td>1</td><td>Worker storage = 20 GiB</td><td>Model is 65 GB. Cannot physically fit on the worker. Need 100+ GiB.</td><td class="critical">CRITICAL</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td>ECR image layer = 52 GB</td><td>Cannot bake 65 GB model into container image (AWS hard limit).</td><td class="critical">CRITICAL</td></tr>
<tr><td>3</td><td>ECS Fargate has no GPU</td><td>Fargate does not support GPUs. Must use ECS on EC2 with GPU instances.</td><td class="critical">CRITICAL</td></tr>
<tr><td>4</td><td>No JFrog-to-S3 transfer</td><td>No automated mechanism to move 65 GB from Artifactory to S3.</td><td class="critical">CRITICAL</td></tr>
<tr><td>5</td><td>No tensor parallelism</td><td>Cannot configure multi-GPU inference (TP=2, TP=4 required).</td><td class="high">HIGH</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>AWS EC2 GPU Instance Pricing - us-east-2 (Ohio) On-Demand</h3>
<div class="note"><b>Note:</b> This path currently FAILS due to critical blockers above. Prices show what EC2 GPU instances cost if AEX infrastructure were upgraded. EC2 GPU pricing confirmed identical in us-east-1 and us-east-2 (verified via devzero.io, doit.com).</div>
<table>
<tr><th style="width:14%;">Instance</th><th style="width:5%;">GPUs</th><th style="width:13%;">GPU Type</th><th style="width:10%;">Total VRAM</th><th style="width:13%;">Can Run?</th><th style="width:5%;">TP</th><th style="width:12%;">$/Hour</th><th style="width:14%;">$/Week (168h)</th><th style="width:14%;">$/Month (730h)</th></tr>
<tr><td>g6.12xlarge</td><td>4</td><td>NVIDIA L4</td><td>96 GB</td><td class="warn">Quantized only</td><td>TP=4</td><td><b>$4.6016</b></td><td>$773.07</td><td>$3,359.17</td></tr>
<tr><td>g6.48xlarge</td><td>8</td><td>NVIDIA L4</td><td>192 GB</td><td class="pass">Yes</td><td>TP=4</td><td><b>$13.3504</b></td><td>$2,242.87</td><td>$9,745.79</td></tr>
<tr><td>g5.12xlarge</td><td>4</td><td>NVIDIA A10G</td><td>96 GB</td><td class="warn">Quantized only</td><td>TP=4</td><td><b>$5.672</b></td><td>$952.90</td><td>$4,140.56</td></tr>
<tr><td>g5.48xlarge</td><td>8</td><td>NVIDIA A10G</td><td>192 GB</td><td class="pass">Yes</td><td>TP=4</td><td><b>$16.288</b></td><td>$2,736.38</td><td>$11,890.24</td></tr>
<tr><td>p4d.24xlarge</td><td>8</td><td>NVIDIA A100 40GB</td><td>320 GB</td><td class="pass">Yes</td><td>TP=2</td><td><b>$21.9576</b></td><td>$3,688.88</td><td>$16,029.05</td></tr>
<tr><td>p4de.24xlarge</td><td>8</td><td>NVIDIA A100 80GB</td><td>640 GB</td><td class="pass">Yes (1 GPU)</td><td>TP=1</td><td><b>$27.4471</b></td><td>$4,611.11</td><td>$20,036.38</td></tr>
<tr><td>p5.48xlarge</td><td>8</td><td>NVIDIA H100 80GB</td><td>640 GB</td><td class="pass">Yes (fastest)</td><td>TP=1</td><td><b>$55.04</b></td><td>$9,246.72</td><td>$40,179.20</td></tr>
</table>
<p><b>Verdict: CURRENTLY FAILS</b> - 4 critical blockers. Would need: ECS on EC2 (not Fargate), 200 GiB storage, runtime S3 model pull.</p>


<h2>5. OPTION 3: Amazon Bedrock</h2>
<table>
<tr><th style="width:40%;">Question</th><th style="width:60%;">Answer</th></tr>
<tr><td>Is Gemma 4 31B available on Bedrock?</td><td class="fail">NO</td></tr>
<tr><td>What Gemma versions are available?</td><td>Only Gemma v3 models</td></tr>
<tr><td>Timeline for Gemma 4 support?</td><td>No announcement as of June 2026</td></tr>
</table>
<p><b>Verdict: NOT POSSIBLE</b> - Amazon Bedrock does not support Gemma 4 models.</p>

